# Bokito Platform Knowledge Logging

Whenever new information is learned about the Bokito platform — including features, modules, workflows, SOPs, business rules, configuration options, user flows, data models, integrations, or pricing — **update `BOKITO_KNOWLEDGE.md`** in the project root immediately.

## When to update

- A user explains how a feature works or is configured
- A new module, page, or capability is discussed
- A business rule or SOP is mentioned
- A workflow or user flow is clarified
- A limitation or edge case is discovered
- Integration behavior is described

## How to update

1. Find the most relevant section in `BOKITO_KNOWLEDGE.md`
2. Add the new knowledge under that section (create a new section if none fits)
3. Be concise and factual — write like internal product documentation
4. Never duplicate existing entries; update them instead
5. Always use present tense ("Users can...", "The system...")
6. User-facing how-to (steps, UI labels, screenshots) belongs in
   `docs/product-help/`, not only here. See `.cursor/rules/product-help-docs.mdc`.

## File location

`BOKITO_KNOWLEDGE.md` in the project root (`c:\Users\Test\Documents\Coding\Bokito-ai chat\BOKITO_KNOWLEDGE.md`)
